instrument wingie
; wingie-proc-glass-cloud — line in as hi-fi grains: a cloud, a slow-motion replay, a
; photograph that breathes. Set the Line/Mic switch to line and play anything into it.
;
; every scene:
;   fader1 (Mix)     how much is happening (grain density, or how fast time runs)
;   fader2 (Decay)   how long each thing lasts (grain size, smear, drift)
;   fader3 (Volume)  where in the past the grains read, or how much of the room
;   keys1            the pitch the grains are played at; octave1 throws it an octave down or up
;   mode1            held: the tape stops and what is in it goes on (freeze / hold / capture)
;   left LED         how loud the line in is;  right LED  how loud what comes out is
; Step through the scenes with a held Mode button and a tap on the other.

the bead curtain
----------------
; grains of the last 0.4 s spread wide; the louder you play the denser they fall. Hold mode2
; and the whole curtain jumps an octave up. keys2 held lets the room behind the grains back
; into the tape, so the curtain feeds on itself; let go and it dries.
the ear is follower attack=0.005 release=0.4
the g is grains 4 window=hann spread=0.7 spray=0.05
the oct1 is transpose
the air is diffuser amount=0.6
the room is reverblite 3 size=0.7
the back is vca
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> ear g
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> g.pitch
mode2 -> g.pitch                  ; held: an octave up
mode1 -> g.freeze
fader1 -> g.density
ear -40> g.density                ; play harder, more grains
fader2 -> g.size
fader3 -> g.position
ear -20> g.spray                  ; a loud phrase scatters them further back
g.left g.right ~> air
air -> room
room -> back
keys2.gate => back.gain            ; the room back into the tape while a top key is held
back -35> g
g.left room -30> guardl
g.right room -30> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
line.both -> lights.left
guardl -> lights.right

slow motion
-----------
; the line in replayed slower and slower without the pitch falling (WSOLA), then smeared
; across the spectrum. fader1 is the speed (down: time stands still), fader2 the smear,
; mode1 holds the tape and loops; a top key held smears to a still wash; key12 (the bottom B)
; plays the replay backwards. Hold mode2 and the wash runs back into the replay, round and
; round, a little darker each time.
the slow is stretch 3 samplerate=quarter
the wash is smear samplerate=quarter blur=0.1
the oct1 is transpose
the back is vca
the rev is attenuverter amount=-1

line.both -> slow
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
oct1 -> slow.pitch
fader1 -> slow.speed
key12 -> rev
rev -120> slow.speed              ; backwards while B is held
mode1 -> slow.hold
slow -> wash
fader2 -> wash.blur
keys2.gate -> wash.blur
wash -> back
mode2 => back.gain
back -40> slow                    ; the wash back into the replay while mode2 is held
slow -70> out
wash -> out
line.both -> lights.left
wash -> lights.right

the photograph that breathes
----------------------------
; a tap on mode1 holds the last moment as a seamless drone; hold mode2 and every attack in the
; line in takes a new photograph by itself; any bottom key takes one too. A swarm of tiny
; grains reads the drone again at the keys' pitch; key1 (bottom C) held sets the swarm loose.
; fader1 from the line to the photograph, fader2 how restless it breathes, fader3 how many
; insects swarm above it.
the photo is grainfreeze 3 samplerate=quarter
the ear is follower attack=0.002 release=0.15
the hit is trigger
the only is vca
the bugs is swarm chaos=0.2 samplerate=quarter
the oct1 is transpose
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> photo ear
ear.gate -> hit
hit -> only                       ; an attack, let through only while mode2 is held
mode2 -> only.gain
mode1.tap only keys1.trig -> photo.capture
fader1 -> photo.blend
fader2 -> photo.drift
octave1 -> oct1
keys1.pitch -> oct1.pitch
photo.left photo.right -> bugs
oct1 -> bugs.pitch
fader3 -> bugs.density
key1 -> bugs.chaos
photo.left bugs.left -> guardl
photo.right bugs.right -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
ear -> lights.left
photo.left -> lights.right

glass rain
----------
; grains that glide in pitch as they sound, falling or rising by as much as keys2 says
; (C none, B almost an octave); octave2 sends them the other way. A pair of insects swarms
; around them out of the same line in. fader1 density, fader2 grain size, fader3 the swarm.
; mode1 held lets the swarm loose (chaos), mode2 held ducks the room away.
the swallows are glisson 3 samplerate=half window=gauss spread=0.5
the bugs is swarm chaos=0.3
the dir is transpose
the room is reverblite 3 size=0.6
the dry is ducker
the guardl is limiter ceiling=0.9
the guardr is limiter ceiling=0.9

line.both -> swallows bugs
octave2 -> dir
keys2.key -> dir.pitch
dir -> swallows.glide
fader1 -> swallows.density
fader2 -> swallows.size
fader3 -> bugs.density
mode1 -> bugs.chaos
swallows.left swallows.right bugs.left bugs.right ~> room
room -> dry
mode2 -> dry.side                 ; held: the room ducks away
swallows.left bugs.left dry -> guardl
swallows.right bugs.right dry -> guardr
guardl -> left
guardr -> right
line.both -> lights.left
swallows.left -> lights.right
